  "prompt": "Find the common rule that maps an input grid to an output grid, given the examples below. Generate a python script that takes a grid as input and transforms it according to the this rule. Anticipate that this program will be applied to several grids, not only the shown test grid.\n\nYour script must define exactly one callable entrypoint:\ndef solve(grid):\nwhere `grid` is passed as a list of lists of integers (list[list[int]]) and the function returns the transformed grid in the same format.\n\nExample 1:\n\nInput:\n4 4 0 0 0 0 5 0\n4 4 0 0 0 0 0 0\n0 0 4 0 0 0 5 0\n0 4 0 0 5 5 0 0\n0 0 6 0 0 0 9 0\n6 6 6 0 0 0 0 9\n6 0 6 6 9 9 0 0\n0 6 6 0 9 0 0 0\nOutput:\n4 4 5 0\n6 6 6 9\n6 9 5 6\n5 5 6 0\n\nExample 2:\n\nInput:\n4 0 0 4 5 5 0 0\n0 0 0 0 0 0 5 5\n4 4 0 4 0 5 0 0\n4 0 4 4 0 5 5 5\n0 0 0 6 0 9 0 9\n0 0 6 0 0 9 0 0\n6 0 0 6 0 9 0 9\n0 0 6 6 0 0 0 9\nOutput:\n5 5 0 6\n0 9 5 5\n6 5 0 6\n4 5 5 5\n\nExample 3:\n\nInput:\n0 0 0 4 5 0 0 0\n4 0 0 0 0 5 0 0\n0 0 0 4 0 0 5 0\n0 4 0 4 0 0 5 0\n6 0 0 0 0 9 9 0\n6 0 0 0 0 9 0 9\n6 0 6 0 9 9 9 0\n6 0 6 0 0 0 0 0\nOutput:\n5 9 9 4\n6 5 0 9\n6 9 5 4\n6 4 5 4\n\nExample 4:\n\nInput:\n4 0 0 4 0 5 0 5\n0 0 4 0 5 0 0 5\n0 0 4 4 0 0 5 5\n4 0 0 0 5 0 0 5\n6 6 6 0 9 0 9 9\n6 6 6 0 0 9 9 9\n6 0 0 6 9 9 0 9\n6 6 0 6 9 0 9 9\nOutput:\n6 5 6 5\n5 6 6 5\n6 9 5 5\n5 6 9 5\n\nExample 5:\n\nInput:\n0 4 4 4 0 5 5 5\n0 0 4 0 5 5 0 5\n0 0 0 0 5 0 0 0\n4 0 0 0 5 0 0 0\n6 6 0 6 0 0 9 9\n0 0 0 6 9 0 9 0\n0 0 0 6 9 0 9 9\n6 6 0 6 0 9 0 9\nOutput:\n6 5 5 5\n5 5 9 5\n5 0 9 6\n5 6 0 6\n\nBelow is a test input grid.\n\nInput:\n0 4 0 4 5 0 0 0\n0 4 4 4 5 0 5 5\n4 4 4 0 0 5 5 5\n0 0 0 0 5 0 0 0\n6 0 6 6 9 9 9 0\n0 0 0 6 0 9 0 0\n0 6 0 0 0 0 9 9\n6 0 0 0 0 9 0 0\n\nYour final answer should just be the python script itself, no other text or markdown.",
  "raw_response": "def solve(grid):\n    \"\"\"\n    Transforms an 8\u00d78 (or any 2N\u00d72N) input grid into an N\u00d7N output grid.\n    For each position (i, j) in the output (0\u2011based, N = len(grid)//2):\n        - TL = grid[i][j]                     # top\u2011left quadrant\n        - TR = grid[i][j + N]                 # top\u2011right quadrant\n        - BL = grid[i + N][j]                 # bottom\u2011left quadrant\n        - BR = grid[i + N][j + N]             # bottom\u2011right quadrant\n    The output cell is the first non\u2011zero value among\n    TR, BL, BR, TL (priority order). If all four are zero, the output is 0.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(grid)\n    half = n // 2\n    out = []\n\n    for i in range(half):\n        row = []\n        for j in range(half):\n            tl = grid[i][j]\n            tr = grid[i][j + half]\n            bl = grid[i + half][j]\n            br = grid[i + half][j + half]\n\n            # priority: TR \u2192 BL \u2192 BR \u2192 TL\n            if tr != 0:\n                val = tr\n            elif bl != 0:\n                val = bl\n            elif br != 0:\n                val = br\n            elif tl != 0:\n                val = tl\n            else:\n                val = 0\n            row.append(val)\n        out.append(row)\n\n    return out",
  "script": "def solve(grid):\n    \"\"\"\n    Transforms an 8\u00d78 (or any 2N\u00d72N) input grid into an N\u00d7N output grid.\n    For each position (i, j) in the output (0\u2011based, N = len(grid)//2):\n        - TL = grid[i][j]                     # top\u2011left quadrant\n        - TR = grid[i][j + N]                 # top\u2011right quadrant\n        - BL = grid[i + N][j]                 # bottom\u2011left quadrant\n        - BR = grid[i + N][j + N]             # bottom\u2011right quadrant\n    The output cell is the first non\u2011zero value among\n    TR, BL, BR, TL (priority order). If all four are zero, the output is 0.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(grid)\n    half = n // 2\n    out = []\n\n    for i in range(half):\n        row = []\n        for j in range(half):\n            tl = grid[i][j]\n            tr = grid[i][j + half]\n            bl = grid[i + half][j]\n            br = grid[i + half][j + half]\n\n            # priority: TR \u2192 BL \u2192 BR \u2192 TL\n            if tr != 0:\n                val = tr\n            elif bl != 0:\n                val = bl\n            elif br != 0:\n                val = br\n            elif tl != 0:\n                val = tl\n            else:\n                val = 0\n            row.append(val)\n        out.append(row)\n\n    return out",
